; The event trace (R1.5 criterion 10, design decision D-11): the steps of
; one component, one record per line. Codec:
; crates/dp-formats/src/trace.rs (`Record`). A record is a canonical
; S-expression; an input or the effects may hold line feeds, so a reader
; finds the end of a record by its lengths.

trace           = *( record LF )
record          = "(" %s"5:trace"
                      text                 ; the component
                      number               ; the number of the step, from 1
                      text                 ; the action of the TLA+ specification
                      number               ; the component's clock in microseconds
                      text                 ; the input of the step
                      text                 ; its effects; empty where none are recorded
                  ")"
LF              = %x0A

; Shared rules. Every value is a canonical S-expression
; (canonical-sexp.abnf): an atom is its length in decimal, a colon and
; that many octets; a list has no whitespace between its items.

number  = atom                        ; its octets are a decimal number below 2^64 without leading zeros
text    = atom                        ; its octets are UTF-8
bytes   = atom
atom    = length ":" *OCTET           ; exactly <length> octets follow the colon
length  = "0" / (%x31-39 *DIGIT)
DIGIT   = %x30-39
OCTET   = %x00-FF
